From b8cf70a524ee87058ddc8063c5b98b4bb6d44bc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bringup <bringup@local>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:50:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 04/38] experiments: archive LogExport design (not built)

Preserves the verified parts of the USB log-export attempt:
- RAM log capture (documented in log-capture.txt, was working)
- FAT16 disk image generator + fixed BOOTLOG.TXT offset 0xC200
- RAM-backed BlockIo driver (reached BLOCK_IO=1 / SIMPLE_FS=1 on device)

Not wired into DSC/FDF/APRIORI on purpose: installing a BlockIo during
APRIORI made the BDS Boot Manager unreachable, and the USB handoff cannot
succeed until EFI_USBFN_IO_PROTOCOL exists.

Also records Phase-1 SPMI static analysis results.
